{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-122648-r4605228","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Latino Scramble","sourcePageId":122648,"sourceRevision":"4605228","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-12-03T21:55:41Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Latino%20Scramble&oldid=4605228","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:20.077Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Breakfast recipes","Category:Colombian recipes","Category:Pan fried recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using corn","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ham","Category:Recipes using ketchup","Category:Recipes using low-moisture mozzarella","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Southwestern recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"1001ad84787a887f9a73284d04bbd795450ca49d8f953a773aa94a9d1b74a04f","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Breakfast recipes|servings=6|time=10 minutes|difficulty=1\n| Image = [[Image:Latino_Scramble.jpg|300px]]\n}}{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Colombia|Colombia]] | [[Cookbook:Breakfast Recipes|Breakfast]]\n\n'''Latino scramble''' is a delicious breakfast option, to feel in a warm tropical morning. You can have this breakfast with [[Cookbook:Cheese|white cheese]]-topped corn arepas, 100% Colombian [[Cookbook:coffee|coffee]], and [[Cookbook:Orange|orange juice]].\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]] \n* 1 large [[Cookbook:onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 1 large [[Cookbook:tomato|tomato]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* 6 [[Cookbook:ham|ham]] slices, chopped\n* 100 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Grating|grated]] [[Cookbook:Mozzarella Cheese|mozzarella cheese]] \n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:butter|butter]]\n* [[Cookbook:salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:pepper|Pepper]]\n* [[Cookbook:Tabasco Sauce|Tabasco sauce]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]]\n* 15 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] (425 g) sweet [[Cookbook:Corn|corn]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Melt butter in a medium [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]] over medium heat.\n# Add the chopped onions, and [[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] until they start to brown.\n# Add ham and sweet corn, and let fry for 5 minutes.\n# Add tomato, salt, and pepper. Though not traditional, you can also add one drop of Tabasco per egg.\n# Beat the eggs with ketchup, and add to frying pan. Immediately add mozzarella cheese.\n# Let cook to your desired egg texture.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* You can add cooked white rice (it gives a feeling of a typical [[Cookbook:Calentao|calentao]]) and diced cooked [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]].\n\n\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ham]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn]]\n[[Category:Breakfast recipes]]\n[[Category:Colombian recipes]]\n[[Category:Southwestern recipes]]\n[[Category:Pan fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using low-moisture mozzarella]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Latino Scramble","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"6 